+of the registered isolated `server-router` VM, bound to this run's UUID
+and outer/manifest hashes. The controller uses QGA to read the SSH key
+advertised on loopback in that guest and compares its Ed25519 fingerprint
+with the configured lab SSH pin. External server JSON receipts are rejected.
+A successful release gate writes
 `exports/<run-id>/publishable.json` with the same outer SHA-256. Candidate mode
 may be used for a thin iteration of selected products; it reports
 `candidate_passed` only and never writes a publishable marker or claims
 `release_passed`.
 
+Pass the original physical Android acquisition to the release gate with
+`gate --run-id <run-id> --lane release --android-real-device-export <path>`.
+The gate verifies the signature, freshness, real-device role, and exact
+planned manifest, outer installer, and platform artifact identities.
+Publication validation and the remaining guest checks still apply.
+
+### Coordinated release authorization
+
+The coordinated gate verifies an exact held installer against the four original
+signed platform exports, their recorded N-1 inputs, and a fresh detached full
+approval. It also requires an owned PowerShell Direct transaction from the
+exact production client and a separate installer-driven publication on the
+isolated lab SSH profile. Both publication runs must complete and pass their
+cleanup checks. The PowerShell Direct transport requires no relay registration
+on the Windows host.
+
+An optional `renewal` in the plan pins a fresh signed approval for the same
+four original exports and the same release bytes. The approval pinned in
+`approval` must have covered the original exact publication from dispatch
+through readback. The gate verifies both signatures and records both hashes.
+
+Run `python3 -B -m deploy.release_lab.coordinated_release_promote verify` with
+`--plan` and `--expected-plan-sha256` as the existing Ubuntu laboratory account.
+The `promote` action revalidates that plan, records the coordinated authorization,
+and copies only the exact held bytes into `dist/selfhosted-windows-client`.
+It does not start the installer. The user starts the final installer manually.
+
 `reset` can remove only an overlay carrying the run/profile ownership marker.
 It refuses base, foreign, production, or unmarked paths.
 
